        "title": "British-German defence startup Hypersonica raises €100M",
        "url": "https://tech.eu/2026/11/02/british-german-defence-startup-hypersonica-raises-eur100m/",
        "publishedOn": "2026-11-02"
      },
      "text": "Hypersonica has raised €100m to build hypersonic deep-strike missiles, nine months after a €23.2m Series A. It is headquartered in Munich with a subsidiary in London, which is the point rather than an accident of incorporation, because the capability it is aiming at by 2029 sits inside the long-range weapons agreement the two governments signed. Lightspeed and General Catalyst co-led, with Plural and 201 Ventures following on from the Series A. Philipp Kerth and Marc Ewenz founded the company in 2023 and say the money goes to testing and to hundreds of engineering and manufacturing jobs in both countries.",
      "note": {
        "text": "Headquartered in Munich with a subsidiary in London, and described by the source as British-German.",
