        "title": "German aerospace startup VÆRIDION raises €30M for zero-emission regional flights",
        "url": "https://tech.eu/2026/11/05/german-aerospace-startup-v-ridion-raises-30m-for-zero-emission-regional-fights/",
        "publishedOn": "2026-11-05"
      },
      "text": "VÆRIDION has raised €30m for the Microliner, a battery-electric nine-seater built for routes of up to 400km. The bet is that the hard part of regional aviation is not the aircraft but the airfields, and that something quiet and electric can use the small ones a jet cannot. SHIFT Invest and Invest-NL co-led the Series A2 from the Netherlands, with World Fund, Project A and Vsquared Ventures following. Ivor van Dartel and Sebastian Seemann left Airbus to start the company in 2021 and are targeting commercial service in 2030, testing at Oberpfaffenhofen in the meantime.",
      "note": {
        "text": "The EU separately selected the company for a €94.5m Innovation Fund grant, which is not equity and is not counted in this round.",
        "source": {
          "publication": "Tech.eu",
          "title": "German aerospace startup VÆRIDION raises €30M for zero-emission regional flights",
